      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "When should a marketing agency pick Pastel or SureFeedback over the other tools on this list?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Pick Pastel if your priority is getting clients commenting on a live site in a few clicks with zero setup friction and you have no need for automated QA or compliance documentation. Pick SureFeedback if you run a WordPress-only shop, want a self-hosted plugin with fixed annual pricing, and data ownership matters more to you than feature depth or two-way PM sync."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does \"AI QA agents running on every deploy\" actually mean in practice?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "When you push a site change, Superflow's AI agents automatically run your QA checklist on the updated live site across desktop and mobile, covering broken links, spelling errors, accessibility issues, mobile layout problems, and custom brand rules. They post findings as pinned comments on the exact elements before any human opens the project. Your team then approves the findings, and the client signs off from a link (no login on Scale and up). In the other tools on this list, a person starts the QA pass, or it runs on a schedule, not on every deploy."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which design review tools on this list work for agencies with healthcare or compliance-driven clients?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Only Superflow publicly documents HIPAA with BAA availability (Enterprise plan). That makes it the only option in this group for agencies that need to sign a Business Associate Agreement. Frame.io and Filestage hold SOC 2 Type II certification. Filestage also carries ISO 27001 with German-hosted servers for European data residency. Superflow, Atarim, and Pastel list SOC 2 on their Enterprise plans."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can my clients leave feedback on a live website without creating an account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, with Superflow clients approve and comment from a shared link with no login or account required on their end. Pastel and SureFeedback also allow no-login client access, while Frame.io requires account creation on some plan tiers."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is per-client Memory in a design review tool and why does it matter for agencies?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Per-client Memory means the review system retains each client's brand rules, past decisions, and learned preferences across every project, so agents apply those rules automatically without you re-entering them each time. In Superflow, Memory compounds over time, meaning by project ten the AI already knows what took project one several rounds to establish. No other tool in this category offers this feature."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do agency design workflow tools handle version control when clients keep requesting changes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The best tools preserve all comments across every version so feedback from round one is still visible when you're on round five. Superflow maintains comment history across versions, which means no feedback gets lost between 'final' and 'final final' states — a common source of rework at agencies."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the fastest way to get a client commenting on a live site with zero setup?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Pastel is the fastest option: paste a URL, share the link, and your client can start commenting with no install, code snippet, or browser extension required. The tradeoff is that Pastel has no automated QA layer, so a human still needs to catch issues before the client sees the site."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Should I use a flat-rate or per-credit pricing model for AI-assisted client feedback management?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Choose flat-rate if you run frequent deploys or monitor multiple sites, since Superflow's $14/site/month bulk option covers unlimited scans regardless of site size. Use per-credit pricing if your project load is unpredictable or you only need occasional AI scans, where à la carte credits starting at 1 credit per single page give you tighter cost control."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which client feedback management tools offer two-way sync with project management software like Asana or Jira?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow offers two-way sync with Asana, Monday.com, ClickUp, Trello, and Jira, meaning comments create tasks and sign-offs close them automatically. Filestage syncs with Jira and Monday.com on higher plans, while Pastel only exports comments one-way and SureFeedback has no PM sync at all."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What marketing agency collaboration tools support Lottie file review alongside websites and video?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow is the only tool in this category that supports Lottie file review alongside websites, video, PDFs, and images in a single workspace. All other tools reviewed here — Atarim, Pastel, Filestage, Frame.io, and SureFeedback — do not support Lottie files."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is there a design review tool that works for agencies on Webflow, Framer, and Shopify, not just WordPress?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Superflow installs on Webflow, Framer, Shopify, WordPress, Wix, Bubble, Squarespace, HubSpot, and plain HTML sites via a one-click integration or snippet. Atarim and SureFeedback are built primarily for WordPress, so multi-CMS agencies will hit real limitations with either of those tools."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I know if my agency actually needs AI QA agents or if manual review is good enough?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If your team is catching the same categories of errors repeatedly across projects — broken links, spelling mistakes, mobile layout issues — that's a signal that manual review is absorbing time that automation could handle. AI QA agents pay off most when you're managing several active client projects at once and a missed error reaching production carries real cost, either in client trust or rework hours."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the difference between how Atarim and Superflow run AI checks on client sites?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Atarim's AI agents run on metered monthly credits, so checks are triggered manually rather than firing automatically on every deploy. Superflow's agents run on every site change without a human initiating the pass, posting findings before anyone opens the project. For agencies shipping frequent updates across multiple clients, that trigger difference changes how many issues get caught before a client sees them."
      }
    }
  ],
  "url": "https://usesuperflow.ai/blog/best-review-platforms-for-agencies",
  "dateModified": "2026-10-31T00:29:32.501Z",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
